    ('kex_not_finalised_by_libssh_server_mapper_expected_sshmessage_kexecdhreply', 'claim:server:L:mapper_expected_sshmessage_kexecdhreply', 'HARNESS', 'server role: GATE 0 -- APPARATUS, not a library divergence. The bucket NAME is kept so it still matches the on-disk corpus directory, but the name is misleading: libssh refuses nothing here. The recorded error mapper_expected_sshmessage_kexecdhreply is manufactured by ssh_rootcause.error_class() from the sshpuffin prefixes "error executing a function symbol" and "error evaluating a term" -- a term-evaluation failure in our own harness, not a libssh protocol error. Swept over all 26 libssh-attributed mapper_* buckets (498 sampled per-PUT logs): 498 apparatus, 0 native libssh errors. wolfSSH hits the SAME term-evaluation failure (597/597), so no stack tolerated it; and the input is canonical in about 70%% of sampled traces rather than fuzzed. The diff shape is uniform in 412/412 sampled: Claims.DifferentTypes(SshClaimInner) + Knowledges.DifferentTypes(AlignedTranscript, source: Decryption) -- our decryption/alignment layer produced an aligned transcript for one PUT and not the other. An earlier revision of this row read "libssh refuses a fuzzed KEX-phase input the other stack tolerated", which is false in all three of its clauses.', 20081),
    ('wolfssh_aead_reject_wrong_invocation_counter_server', 'aead:server:wrong_invocation_counter', 'KNOWN-CVE', "The packet wolfSSH rejects carries an explicit AES-GCM INVOCATION COUNTER (the mutator replaced the fn_u32_auto sentinel) whose value differs from that packet's true index since the last NEWKEYS, so the GCM nonce is wrong and the tag MUST fail; wolfSSH's tag failure is correct. libssh 0.11.4 does not reject it: its OpenSSL AES-GCM decrypt path (src/libcrypto.c:734-740, identical to the pristine 0.11.4 release) treats only rc < 0 from EVP_DecryptFinal as failure, but EVP_DecryptFinal returns 0 on a tag mismatch, so the failure is ignored and the unauthenticated plaintext is processed. This is the KNOWN CVE-2026-59847 (libssh 0.9.0-0.12.0, CVSS 6.5, fixed in 0.11.5/0.12.1; libssh advisory 2026-07-21), rediscovered here through the differential. Confirmed on a trace with a libssh packet-log build: libssh decrypts the wrong-key packet to garbage (type 37) and dispatches it.", 19976),
