    ('harness_wolfssh_premature_auth_claim', 'named:harness_wolfssh_premature_auth_claim', 'HARNESS', "The wolfSSH harness emits its publickey auth claim before wolfSSH verifies the signature; wolfSSH's own wire says USERAUTH_FAILURE. Claim-oracle artefact, not an auth divergence.", 15481),
    ('wolfssh_server_rejects_first_gerr1089_unable_to_match_user_auth_key_type', 'status:server:W:wolfssh_gerr1089', 'BENIGN', "server role: wolfSSH is the first PUT to stop, with gerr1089_unable_to_match_user_auth_key_type (a defensive/parsing check on a fuzzed input); libssh gets further on the same input. Auth-symmetric or asymmetry explained by the earlier stop (guarded). NOTE -- the error text 'unable to match user auth key type' in this bucket's NAME is wolfSSH's own string for WS_MATCH_UA_KEY_ID_E and it is MISLEADING: -1089 has exactly one raise site in the wolfSSH tree, DoExtInfoServerSigAlgs (internal.c:6806), and is never raised on a credential. It fires when an EXT_INFO 'server-sig-algs' value matches no algorithm -- an extension RFC 8308 s3.1 defines as server-to-client, which DoExtInfo parses with no role check. Measured over all 16,348 corpus traces that hit -1089: wolfSSH's failing step is an fn_ext_info in 16,348/16,348 (100%). The behaviour is therefore present in ALL of them, not only in the 852 that additionally show an authentication divergence and are named known_wolfssh_aborts_on_unusable_server_sig_algs -- that conjunct is a fact about libssh's progress, not about wolfSSH's conformance. See that bucket for the analysis.", 15308),
    ('wolfssh_aead_reject_plaintext_after_newkeys_client', 'aead:client:plaintext_after_newkeys', 'BENIGN-ARTEFACT', "The attacker sends an UNENCRYPTED packet after NEWKEYS; wolfSSH tries to AEAD-decrypt it and fails (gerr=-180) - correct. libssh waits for the tag bytes the plaintext packet lacks (packet log: 'processed 0 bytes' until close) and the harness reports that silence as success: a measurement artefact, not acceptance. (Once more bytes arrive libssh would not detect the tag mismatch either - CVE-2026-59847 - but this corpus shows it stalling.)", 14609),
    ('known_wolfssh_client_accepts_unsolicited_userauth_success', 'named:known_wolfssh_client_accepts_unsolicited_userauth_success', 'FINDING-LOW', 'wolfSSH CLIENT treats a USERAUTH_SUCCESS that arrives before any SERVICE_ACCEPT (i.e. before it sent an auth request) as authentication, then sends a method-"none" USERAUTH_REQUEST and opens a channel without awaiting a reply; the libssh client refuses the message (packet.c:588). Library defect (wolfSSH ssh.c connect ladder + DoUserAuthSuccess has no state check), present on master. Only the keyed peer can send it (post-NEWKEYS AEAD); no credential is sent.', 13617),
    ('wolfssh_client_rejects_first_gerr1007_would_overflow_if_continued_failure', 'status:client:W:wolfssh_gerr1007', 'BENIGN', 'client role: wolfSSH is the first PUT to stop, with gerr1007_would_overflow_if_continued_failure (a defensive/parsing check on a fuzzed input); libssh gets further on the same input. Auth-symmetric or asymmetry explained by the earlier stop (guarded).', 13591),
