    ('harness_libssh_channel_request_types_unhandled', 'named:harness_libssh_channel_request_types_unhandled', 'HARNESS', 'CHANNEL_REQUEST of a type the sshpuffin libssh harness registers no callback for (pty-req, env, subsystem...): libssh answers CHANNEL_FAILURE, wolfSSH SUCCESS. Harness coverage (Gate 0).', 4675),
    ('transcript_server_first_libssh_none_wolfssh_93', 'shape:server:L-/W93', 'BENIGN', 'server role, transcript-only divergence (no status or claim difference): at the first point where the two decrypted transcripts differ, libssh sent nothing and wolfSSH 93(CHANNEL_WINDOW_ADJUST). Connection-protocol reply presence/count/order/content latitude; authentication agrees (guarded).', 4430),
    ('transcript_server_first_libssh_82_wolfssh_92', 'shape:server:L82/W92', 'BENIGN', 'server role, transcript-only divergence (no status or claim difference): at the first point where the two decrypted transcripts differ, libssh sent 82(REQUEST_FAILURE) and wolfSSH 92(CHANNEL_OPEN_FAILURE). Connection-protocol reply presence/count/order/content latitude; authentication agrees (guarded).', 4390),
    ('wolfssh_aead_reject_wrong_invocation_counter_client', 'aead:client:wrong_invocation_counter', 'KNOWN-CVE', "The packet wolfSSH rejects carries an explicit AES-GCM INVOCATION COUNTER (the mutator replaced the fn_u32_auto sentinel) whose value differs from that packet's true index since the last NEWKEYS, so the GCM nonce is wrong and the tag MUST fail; wolfSSH's tag failure is correct. libssh 0.11.4 does not reject it: its OpenSSL AES-GCM decrypt path (src/libcrypto.c:734-740, identical to the pristine 0.11.4 release) treats only rc < 0 from EVP_DecryptFinal as failure, but EVP_DecryptFinal returns 0 on a tag mismatch, so the failure is ignored and the unauthenticated plaintext is processed. This is the KNOWN CVE-2026-59847 (libssh 0.9.0-0.12.0, CVSS 6.5, fixed in 0.11.5/0.12.1; libssh advisory 2026-07-21), rediscovered here through the differential. Confirmed on a trace with a libssh packet-log build: libssh decrypts the wrong-key packet to garbage (type 37) and dispatches it.", 4144),
