    ('known_libssh_cve_2026_59847_authenticates_on_tag_failed_packet', 'named:known_libssh_cve_2026_59847_authenticates_on_tag_failed_packet', 'KNOWN-CVE', "The client's USERAUTH_REQUEST is itself encrypted under a wrong key/nonce: wolfSSH rejects it with an AES-GCM tag failure (gerr=-180), libssh ACCEPTS it and answers USERAUTH_SUCCESS. libssh 0.11.4 ignores AES-GCM tag failures (src/libcrypto.c:737 checks EVP_DecryptFinal rc < 0, which never holds): KNOWN CVE-2026-59847 (fixed 0.11.5/0.12.1), here observed at the authentication step. Integrity-only: the credential/signature inside is the attacker's own valid one, so no party without credentials authenticates; it shows libssh acting on an unauthenticated ciphertext.", 419),
