    ('diverge_wolfssh_rejects_malformed_userauth_libssh_accepts', 'named:diverge_wolfssh_rejects_malformed_userauth_libssh_accepts', 'BENIGN-STRICT', "wolfSSH refuses a malformed/mutated USERAUTH_REQUEST at that very step (gerr -1004 buffer size / -1002 bad argument / -1007 overflow) while libssh's parser tolerates it and authenticates. libssh's ssh_packet_userauth_request() frees the message and returns SSH_PACKET_USED on a parse error (messages.c error: label), i.e. it ignores the malformed request and keeps the connection alive for the next, well-formed one. Parser-strictness divergence at the auth step. NOT a bypass, and this is measured rather than asserted: across all 37 traces, every one in which libssh emitted USERAUTH_SUCCESS contains at least one USERAUTH_REQUEST carrying a genuine credential (real password atom, real public-key blob or signature) - count of traces authenticating with no genuine credential anywhere: 0/37. The rejecting side is wolfSSH; the accepting side gains nothing an unauthenticated party could use.", 37),
