    ('kex_not_finalised_by_libssh_client_mapper_other', 'claim:client:L:mapper_other', 'HARNESS', 'client role: GATE 0 -- APPARATUS, not a library divergence. The bucket NAME is kept so it still matches the on-disk corpus directory, but the name is misleading: libssh refuses nothing here. The recorded error mapper_other is manufactured by ssh_rootcause.error_class() from the sshpuffin prefixes "error executing a function symbol" and "error evaluating a term" -- a term-evaluation failure in our own harness, not a libssh protocol error. Swept over all 26 libssh-attributed mapper_* buckets (498 sampled per-PUT logs): 498 apparatus, 0 native libssh errors. wolfSSH hits the SAME term-evaluation failure (597/597), so no stack tolerated it; and the input is canonical in about 70%% of sampled traces rather than fuzzed. The diff shape is uniform in 412/412 sampled: Claims.DifferentTypes(SshClaimInner) + Knowledges.DifferentTypes(AlignedTranscript, source: Decryption) -- our decryption/alignment layer produced an aligned transcript for one PUT and not the other. An earlier revision of this row read "libssh refuses a fuzzed KEX-phase input the other stack tolerated", which is false in all three of its clauses.', 21),
    ('known_libssh_cve_2026_59847_client_enters_authenticated_state', 'named:known_libssh_cve_2026_59847_client_enters_authenticated_state', 'KNOWN-CVE', 'libssh CLIENT enters the AUTHENTICATED state although the peer never sent USERAUTH_SUCCESS. An attacker packet encrypted under a bogus key (key/IV literals instead of the derived schedule) fails its AES-GCM tag; libssh does not reject it (CVE-2026-59847) and parses the resulting garbage as a control message. Witness 20260923-190740214: libssh logs `read type 52 [len=192,padding=-88]` (negative padding = not a well-formed packet), then "Authentication successful", then CHANNEL_OPEN. Scope: an ILLUSTRATION that the integrity defect reaches control-plane decisions, NOT an impact escalation -- an attacker wanting to feed forged data to the client would let auth complete and tamper with CHANNEL_DATA instead (simpler, and the session survives; after a forged SUCCESS the server still rejects the client\'s channels). Verified end-to-end by a keyless one-byte MITM PoC (poc_cve_2026_59847/).', 20),
    ('libssh_server_rejects_first_libssh_incorrect_size_for_server_curve_public_k', 'status:server:L:libssh_incorrect_size_for_server_curve_public_k', 'BENIGN', 'server role: libssh is the first PUT to stop, with its own check libssh_incorrect_size_for_server_curve_public_k; wolfSSH gets further on the same input.', 20),
