    ('wolfssh_aead_reject_computed_counter_term_server', 'aead:server:computed_counter_term', 'KNOWN-CVE', "The AES-GCM invocation counter of the rejected packet is a COMPUTED term rather than the fn_u32_auto sentinel or a constant - e.g. fn_channel_send_budget(fn_decrypted_message(..)) or fn_initial_window_size(fn_channel_open(..)) - so it evaluates to a channel window / packet size, not the packet's index since the last NEWKEYS, and the nonce is wrong. Two shapes: a sentinel BURIED inside such an accessor is never rewritten (renumber_aesgcm_counters matches fn_u32_auto only at the ROOT of the counter argument) and its raw value u32::MAX-1 is used; or the accessor reads a queried message and yields e.g. 32768 where the true index was 3. Not decidable from the term alone, so the rule was verified by execution (PUFFIN_DUMP_KEY) on 100% of the affected traces: the counter actually used is never the true index. wolfSSH's rejection is correct; libssh does not reject it (CVE-2026-59847).", 17),
