    ('wolfssh_client_rejects_first_gerr1089_unable_to_match_user_auth_key_type', 'status:client:W:wolfssh_gerr1089', 'BENIGN', "client role: wolfSSH is the first PUT to stop, with gerr1089_unable_to_match_user_auth_key_type (a defensive/parsing check on a fuzzed input); libssh gets further on the same input. Auth-symmetric or asymmetry explained by the earlier stop (guarded). NOTE -- the error text 'unable to match user auth key type' in this bucket's NAME is wolfSSH's own string for WS_MATCH_UA_KEY_ID_E and it is MISLEADING: -1089 has exactly one raise site in the wolfSSH tree, DoExtInfoServerSigAlgs (internal.c:6806), and is never raised on a credential. It fires when an EXT_INFO 'server-sig-algs' value matches no algorithm -- an extension RFC 8308 s3.1 defines as server-to-client, which DoExtInfo parses with no role check. Measured over all 16,348 corpus traces that hit -1089: wolfSSH's failing step is an fn_ext_info in 16,348/16,348 (100%). The behaviour is therefore present in ALL of them, not only in the 852 that additionally show an authentication divergence and are named known_wolfssh_aborts_on_unusable_server_sig_algs -- that conjunct is a fact about libssh's progress, not about wolfSSH's conformance. See that bucket for the analysis.", 11),
